Analyze this {language} code for sensitive data exposure and logging failures (OWASP A09).

Source file:
{source}

Already reported by mechanical pattern analysis — do NOT report these again:
{known_findings}

Detect:
- Credentials, tokens, keys or personal data written to logs or stdout
- Whole request, response or entity objects logged, carrying secrets as a side effect
- Stack traces, SQL text or internal paths returned to the caller
- Secrets placed in URLs, redirect targets or error messages
- Personal data stored or transmitted without masking, hashing or encryption
- Security-relevant events (auth failure, permission change) not logged at all
- Log statements that an attacker can inject newlines into (log forging)

Return a JSON array of findings. Each finding:
{{
  "exposure_type": "SECRET_IN_LOG|OBJECT_DUMP|INTERNALS_TO_CALLER|SECRET_IN_URL|UNPROTECTED_PII|MISSING_AUDIT_LOG|LOG_FORGING|OTHER",
  "line": <line number>,
  "severity": "high|medium|low",
  "description": "one sentence naming the data exposed and where it goes",
  "fix": "concrete fix suggestion"
}}

Return [] if no issues found. Return ONLY the JSON array, no prose.
